
- Protoss shields visible in jade
- Build revamp. Make them bigger and better
- Zerg hives should have some mycelium around them, to imitate creep
- recipes for buildings
- require pylons
- generally fix unit sizes and hitboxes
- get proper graphics
- add air units
- AI improvements
  - Create build lists telling the enemy what to make. Each line will have a command and then parameters.
  - Parameters may take the form of a comma-delimited list of [Quantity] [Unit] and will be referred to as [UnitList]
  - When instructed to build certain units, the AI will wait until it has the appropriate resources available.
    - [Quantity] can be a range of integers, in which case a number should be randomly selected from that range whne it is executed
  - The following commands should be implemented
    - Workers: [Number]
    The AI will from this point forward make sure it has at minimum this many workers, training new ones when it is below the number
    - Defence: [UnitList]
    The AI will train these units and leave them patrolling the area near the base.
    - Wave: [UnitList]
    The AI will train these units and send them to attack the enemy base once all of them are trained.
    - Wait [Seconds]
    Waits [Seconds] seconds before executing the next command
    - Repeat [Integer]
    Repeats the previous [Integer] commands endlessly

Additional units in old mod:
Protoss: Zealot, Dark Templar, Zeratul, Probe (+Dark/Void/Purifier variants), Reaver, Scarab
Zerg: Zergling family, Hydralisk family, Mutalisk family, Larva/Broodling, Queen, Brutalisk, Tyrannozor, Brakk
Terran: Marine, Civilian/Infested Civilian, Predator, Jim Raynor, Wraith, Scout
Two interesting orphans: Overlord and Sentry have complete, large hand-built models (700-1650 lines) with textures implied but no entity class wiring them up — those could be extracted if you ever want an Overlord or Sentry uni